# Maintain architecture rules

When a change alters structure, contracts, or placement conventions, update `.cursor/rules/` in the **same** task. Stale rules waste tokens and cause wrong edits.

## Update when

- New/renamed folder under `src/`, `core/`, `tools/`
- Visual / design conventions (`concepts/ART_DIRECTION.md`; folder stays AI-only — `concepts.mdc`)
- New feature, event bus, or FSM state
- Feature isolation or `core/` boundary changes
- Scene-isolation / Resource-default contract changes
- Editor-first UI policy changes
- Target platforms or cross-platform playability rules change
- Export ignore folders (`.gdignore` / `export_presets.cfg`)
- HFSM library semantics or JSON config conventions change
- Combat interaction table / pawn lifecycle contracts change
- Entry point or main-scene wiring changes
- A convention in these rules is deliberately broken or replaced

## How

1. Edit the smallest relevant rule file (prefer patch over rewrite).
2. Keep each rule focused; one concern per file.
3. Prefer paths + must/never over prose.
4. If a rule becomes wrong, fix or delete it — never leave contradictions.
5. After structural work, briefly confirm rules still match reality.

## Do not

- Duplicate the same map across many rule files
- Document one-off bugs or temporary hacks as architecture
- Expand rules with unused library details
